The gun is a firearm the [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]] kept at [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], and the artifact [[People/Althane/The Broker|the Broker]] hired [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] to recover. A shot from it once put a hole through the Broker's own body.

[[People/Althane/Karkov|Karkov]] called it the House's best chance at ridding the sphere of outward influence forever. A shot from it leeches the divinity out of whoever it strikes, and the loss does not pass; [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] used it on Karkov to strip his divine power away before he was killed. The Weft took it from Karkov and carried it to the Broker, who used it to close the wound it had dealt him and gave it back, so that it travels with the Weft now.

The House names the weapon the Divinity Leech, and a leech is what sits in its center chamber: a thing that squeals when it is pulled out and glows orange with its own blood. Squeezed, it gives that blood up and loses its hold on whatever it was holding; put back, it regrows and takes hold again. To whom the gun belonged before the House, no one has said. Its work carries a faint likeness to that of [[Geography/Althane/The Hollow/Lava Ruin/Damien|Damien]], as if made by a distant relation.
